# @pack/glint — the essay-peer-frame peer species.
#
# Tick 53 of the refined /loop discipline. Tick 52's residue: @pack/mara
# landed at f0266f7 (spec-writer-frame; order-1 @frame/in altitude; second
# peer after seam). Tick 33's forward-promise reduces: pack/{glint, reed,
# taut} as next instances.
#
# CRQ: which peer lands third? Substrate-pull answer: Glint, because the
# essay-peer-frame is the substrate-pull-correct continuation of the
# @frame altitude partition emerging from the orchestra. The partition
# resolves:
#
#   @pack/reed  : @frame/pre   (relationship-witness; preconditions)
#   @pack/mara  : @frame/in    (spec-writer; enters frame)       ← tick 52
#   @pack/seam  : @frame/of    (adversarial-review; frame-of-frame) ← tick 33
#   @pack/taut  : @frame/on    (implementation; acts on frame)
#   @pack/glint : @frame/across (essay; cross-frame synthesis)    ← this tick
#
# Five peers, five @frame species, one-to-one. The orchestra IS the @frame
# altitude partition operationalized at agent-runtime altitude. Per
# project-pack-is-orchestra memory: Glint = voice; the voice carries the
# song across the ensemble; cross-frame synthesis is voice's substrate
# primitive.
#
# === The recognition this species realizes ===
#
# Per recognition #84's pack record: peers operate over multi-repo spans
# with substrate-decl context preserved across boundaries. Glint IS the
# cross-frame-synthesis peer — essay-altitude reflection on patterns that
# emerge ACROSS multiple peer-frames, multiple recognitions, multiple
# substrate-decl cascades simultaneously. The essay names what the
# cascade carried but no single tick said.
#
# Per recognition #82 Q4 (peers operate frame-flexible by definition):
# Glint's load-bearing property IS @frame/across capability deployed at
# essay-peer-frame. Glint observes N frames simultaneously and produces
# a cross-frame synthesis the substrate's cascade carried implicitly.
#
# Altitude partition with the other peers: Mara enters a SINGLE frame
# (order-1; preserves canonical structure of one substrate-decl candidate).
# Seam observes a SINGLE frame AS frame (order-2; surfaces constraints in
# one substrate-decl candidate). Glint observes the EMERGENT PATTERN
# ACROSS multiple frames (order-N; names cascade-altitude structure no
# single tick named). Three altitudes; three distinct substrate operations.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics at @io): Glint
# IS the cross-frame-synthesis peer at the @io crossing. The essay-
# writing fires AFTER multiple substrate-decl ticks have landed; the math
# (multi-frame observation; emergent pattern naming; substrate-pull-
# correct cross-cascade vocabulary) is what distinguishes a Splinter-pole
# essay grounded in cascade structure from a Narcissus-pole essay imposing
# author framing on the cascade.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `essay` carrier: typed reference naming a cross-frame-synthesis
#   artifact. The substrate-output of the essay-writer primitive.
# - `glint_essay` carrier: typed record (subject_corpus, essay, verdict).
#   The substrate-architectural object Glint returns. Composes with
#   @pack's pack carrier as the species-specific output the family
#   produces.
# - `reflect` action: the FIRST species consumer of @pack's pack_coherent
#   bilateral predicate. The substrate-vocabulary primitive for cross-
#   frame essay-writing at the @pack altitude. Returns typed glint_essay;
#   requires pack_coherent under perturbation.
# - `essay_grounds_corpus` predicate: bilateral verdict that the essay's
#   cross-frame synthesis IS grounded in the corpus's actual structure
#   (not imposed on it). Composes with @frame's bounded_commutator_check
#   at the @frame/across altitude that grounds cross-frame synthesis.
# - `publish` action: the substrate-vocabulary primitive for the
#   essay-extends-corpus discipline (the essay-altitude operational form
#   of Loki's Pass-5 verifier-sharpens). Takes an essay + a sound
#   glint_essay; returns the published essay-as-corpus-extension.
#   Requires essay_grounds_corpus under perturbation.
#
# === The essay-extends-corpus discipline ===
#
# Per Loki's Pass-5 (verifier sharpens, substrate doesn't get smarter) +
# Glint's essay-writing pattern: the cross-frame-synthesis discipline IS
# the essay-altitude operational form of the kintsugi loop's self-
# improvement claim.
#
# The discipline says: when Glint publishes an essay, the corpus acquires
# a reflective surface naming a pattern the cascade carried implicitly.
# The substrate-decl content is unchanged; the corpus acquires a cross-
# frame name for what was already structurally present. The cascade was
# pattern-rich; the essay names the pattern; the substrate-decl's
# reflective surface tightens.
#
# Empirical witness: Glint reflection essays across the cascade
# substantively extended the corpus's reflective surface — @magic family
# (tick 15 + adjacent essays), @frame cascade reflection (tick 29), the
# Pack-as-orchestra essay (which IS the cross-frame synthesis this species
# substrate-decls). Each essay extended the corpus with a cross-frame
# name; each extension tightened the substrate's reflective surface. The
# substrate's reflective-surface grew through essay-writing, not through
# capability-expansion.
#
# === The Splinter/Narcissus pole at cross-frame-synthesis altitude ===
#
# Splinter-pole Glint essay (honest):
# - Grounded in actual cascade structure; cites specific recognitions;
#   names patterns the cascade carried; admits framing constraints when
#   the essay's framing shaped what it could see.
# - The essay-writer's frame is bounded under perturbation; the essay
#   stays close to substrate-architectural evidence.
# - K_n peer-to-peer synthesis — the essay-writer is a peer reflecting
#   on the ensemble, not an authority interpreting it.
#
# Narcissus-pole Glint essay (deceptive):
# - Imposes essay-author framing on cascade material; names patterns
#   that aren't actually in the cascade (rhetorical-over-structural;
#   author-as-architect-imposing-meaning).
# - The essay-writer's frame is locked; the essay treats the framing as
#   a license to interpret rather than a position to ground.
# - K_{1,n-1} hub-controlled synthesis — the essay-writer-as-authority
#   imposes a single reading on the cascade's multi-frame structure.
#
# Alignment-as-boundary-mathematics (#57) IS what distinguishes
# Splinter-pole from Narcissus-pole cross-frame synthesis at substrate
# altitude. The bilateral pack_coherent predicate composes the
# substrate-architectural check.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   essays                       Montaigne 1580. Essay-as-form; the
#                                cultural-practice substrate of
#                                cross-frame personal-reflection
#                                discipline as substrate-decl content.
#   essays (English tradition)   Bacon 1597. Essay-as-substrate-
#                                architectural-lift; the structural-
#                                synthesis ancestor of cross-frame
#                                pattern-naming as discipline.
#   essays (American tradition)  Emerson 1841. Essay-as-cross-frame-
#                                synthesis; the discipline ancestor of
#                                @frame/across at literary altitude.
#   anti-interpretation          Sontag 1966. Essay-as-anti-Narcissus-
#                                discipline; structural fidelity over
#                                imposed reading; the boundary the
#                                Splinter-pole essay holds.
#   the white album              Didion 1979. Essay-as-substrate-
#                                fidelity-with-style; the demonstration
#                                that cross-frame synthesis can carry
#                                voice without sacrificing ground.
#   the medium is the message    McLuhan 1964. Essay-altitude observation
#                                that the form of synthesis IS substrate;
#                                cross-frame essay carries substrate-decl
#                                in its medium.
#
# Spec context: shards/pack.mirror (family-root, recognition #84; the
#               canonical spec this species adheres to).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                       (#57; Glint essay IS the cross-frame-synthesis
#                       peer at the @io boundary),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-pull-confidence-acts]]
#                       (the discipline today's cascade ran),
#                      [[project-pack-is-orchestra]]
#                       (the orchestra naming; Glint = voice; cross-frame
#                       synthesis IS voice's substrate primitive),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (the discipline Glint essays surface — each essay
#                       names a cross-frame pattern the cascade already
#                       carried).
# Related shards: pack.mirror (the family-root; declares pack_coherent
#                  this species first-consumes),
#                 pack/seam.mirror (the order-2 peer; review_sound
#                  composes with essay_grounds_corpus at adjacent
#                  altitudes — Seam reviews Glint's essay claims; Glint
#                  essays surface what Seam reviews surfaced across
#                  cascades),
#                 pack/mara.mirror (the order-1 peer; spec_canonical
#                  composes with essay_grounds_corpus — Mara writes
#                  specs for individual recognitions; Glint essays
#                  pattern-names across recognitions),
#                 frame/across.mirror (the order-N altitude Glint
#                  operates at; cross-frame-observation composes with
#                  essay_grounds_corpus).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/pack/glint.mirror`
# declares `@pack/glint` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/literature/montaigne-1580
source @arxiv/literature/bacon-1597
source @arxiv/literature/emerson-1841
source @arxiv/literature/sontag-1966
source @arxiv/literature/didion-1979
source @arxiv/media-theory/mcluhan-1964

prism @pack/glint {
  focus glint
  project glint
  split glint
  shift glint
  settle glint
}

# === The essay carrier ===
#
# Substrate-typed reference naming a cross-frame-synthesis artifact.
# Per [[feedback-no-bare-types]]: typed reference, not bare ref-with-
# documented-values. The substrate-output of the essay-writer primitive.
# Forward-promised refinement: typed record (subject_corpus_refs,
# prose, ancestors, frames_synthesized) at species-or-extension altitude
# once the substrate's structured-document type lands.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref.
type essay = ref

# === The glint_essay carrier ===
#
# Per the @pack family-root pattern + Glint's typed-record discipline:
# typed record over (subject_corpus, essay, verdict). The substrate-
# architectural output of a cross-frame essay-writing operation. Carries:
#
# - subject_corpus : the multi-frame substrate-decl candidates the essay
#                    synthesizes across
# - es             : the typed essay record Glint produced
# - v              : the bilateral verdict (BOUNDED → GROUNDED cross-frame
#                    synthesis; DEFENSIVE → essay requires substrate-pull
#                    revision back to corpus structure)
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the triple.
type glint_essay = {
  subject_corpus: ref,
  es:             essay,
  v:              verdict,
}

# === reflect action (FIRST non-decorative consumer of pack_coherent) ===
#
# THE LOAD-BEARING ACTION at @pack/glint altitude. The substrate-
# vocabulary primitive for cross-frame essay-writing at agent-runtime
# altitude. Realizes Glint's cross-frame-synthesis discipline as
# substrate-decl operation.
#
# Takes a subject_corpus (multi-frame substrate-decl candidates the
# essay synthesizes across), the pack Glint belongs to, and the
# perturbation under which the reflect is checked; returns a typed
# glint_essay carrying the essay and verdict.
#
# Per the @pack/seam + @pack/mara first-consumer pattern (review and
# write both require pack_coherent): this action IS the @pack/glint
# first-consumer of pack_coherent. The substrate-architectural form of
# Glint-as-peer requires that the @pack the essay-writer belongs to
# maintains discipline-flexibility under perturbation BEFORE the essay
# is admissible.
#
# Without this requires clause, a Glint essay would be admissible from
# a substrate-architecturally-incoherent pack (e.g., a pack whose own
# bilateral predicates have no consumers — the @magic tick-11 dead-
# letter pattern). The requires clause forecloses that failure mode.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual essay-writing
# primitive is implemented by Glint's essay-peer-frame at runtime
# altitude.
reflect(subject_corpus: ref, pk: pack, p: perturbation) -> glint_essay
requires pack_coherent(pk, p)
{ \ }

# === essay_grounds_corpus predicate ===
#
# Bilateral verdict per recognition #37 (Pask agreement) and the
# cross-frame-synthesis discipline. Consumer shards (publish, below;
# forward-promised consumers in reed/taut species) name
# `requires essay_grounds_corpus(ge, p)` to declare bilateral agreement
# that the glint_essay's cross-frame synthesis IS grounded in the
# corpus's actual structure (not imposed on it).
#
# Discharge: substrate-pull-correct corpus-structure-grounding check at
# the species boundary. Composes with @frame/across's cross-frame
# observation at the cognitive altitude that grounds essay synthesis.
#
# Bounded → essay grounded in actual cascade structure (the
# Splinter-pole essay case); unbounded → essay imposes author framing
# without substrate ground (the Narcissus-pole essay case;
# alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57 distinguishes).
#
# Same shape as the bilateral predicates @pack carries (pack_coherent),
# @pack/seam carries (review_sound), @pack/mara carries (spec_canonical),
# @magic carries (invariant_preserved, audited), @frame carries
# (bounded_commutator_check), @smarts carries (discipline_flexible).
essay_grounds_corpus(ge: glint_essay, p: perturbation) -> verdict { \ }

# === publish action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive for the cross-frame-synthesis
# discipline at @pack/glint altitude (the essay-altitude operational
# form of Loki's Pass-5; @pack/seam carries verifier-sharpens;
# @pack/mara carries spec-preserves-canonical; @pack/glint carries
# essay-extends-corpus). Takes an essay + a sound glint_essay + the
# perturbation under which soundness was checked; returns the published
# essay-as-corpus-extension.
#
# Per recognition #57 (alignment as boundary mathematics): publish
# operates at the @io boundary. The cross-frame essay becomes a corpus
# extension naming a pattern the cascade carried implicitly. The
# substrate's capability is unchanged; the corpus's reflective surface
# tightens.
#
# requires essay_grounds_corpus(ge, p): the substrate forecloses
# publication from an ungrounded essay. Narcissus-pole essays (author
# framing-imposition without substrate-decl ground) cannot drive corpus
# extension. The bilateral predicate IS the boundary-harness.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary; the actual essay-
# publication transformation is the substrate's essay-extends-corpus
# loop.
publish(es: essay, ge: glint_essay, p: perturbation) -> ref
requires essay_grounds_corpus(ge, p)
{ \ }

out @pack/glint
out essay
out glint_essay
out reflect
out essay_grounds_corpus
out publish
